<title>USA: Medical Industries president dies.</title>
<headline>Medical Industries president dies.</headline>
<dateline>BOYNTON BEACH, Fla. 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Medical Industries of America Inc said on Wednesday that its president, Harry Kobrin, died of a heart attack.</p>
<p>&quot;We are all deeply saddened by the sudden loss of Harry, especially in light of the dramatic turnaround of events currently underway at Medical Industries,&quot; said Chairman Michael Morrell.</p>
<p>Morrell will assume daily operational control of the company, until the board of directors can find a qualified successor, the company said.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
